Third-party IdP auth in this repo is split between a small shared Go package and a single OAuth2 implementation. Only OAuth2 is implemented and wired at runtime.

## Abstraction package

**Path:** `/bench/repo/internal/idp`  
**Module import:** `github.com/usememos/memos/internal/idp`

This package holds the cross-provider user-info contract used by all IdP integrations:

```1:8:/bench/repo/internal/idp/idp.go
package idp

type IdentityProviderUserInfo struct {
	Identifier  string
	DisplayName string
	Email       string
	AvatarURL   string
}
```

There is no explicit Go `interface` here; the abstraction is the shared `IdentityProviderUserInfo` type that protocol implementations must populate. The SSO resolver consumes that type protocol-agnostically:

```19:19:/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/auth_service_sso.go
func (s *APIV1Service) resolveSSOUser(ctx context.Context, currentUser *store.User, identityProvider *storepb.IdentityProvider, userInfo *idp.IdentityProviderUserInfo) (*store.User, error) {
```

